{
  "paraphrased_text": "The wedding of Norway’s Princess Märtha Louise, a known clairvoyant and the daughter of one of Europe’s most enduring monarchs, to Durek Verrett, a Californian shaman, took place on Saturday in Geiranger under cloudy skies. Despite the unconventional nature of the union, crowds gathered to witness the event. At 52, Märtha Louise—fourth in line to the Norwegian throne—exchanged vows with the 49-year-old Verrett in a traditional Church of Norway ceremony at the upscale Hotel Union, nestled near the Geiranger fjord. The bride was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her daughters, Leah and Emma Behn, from her previous marriage to the late author Ari Behn, which ended in divorce in 2017. Among the 350 guests were prominent royals, such as her brother, Crown Prince Haakon, and his wife, Crown Princess Mette-Marit, as well as Sweden’s Crown Princess Victoria with Prince Daniel, and the Netherlands’ Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien. Märtha Louise’s life has been anything but typical for royalty; she has openly embraced her clairvoyant abilities and previously operated a school focused on angelic communication. In 2022, she decided to withdraw from official royal responsibilities to prioritize her ventures with Verrett and maintain a clearer separation from the Norwegian royal house. Verrett, who refers to himself as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator' on social media, counts Gwyneth Paltrow, founder of Goop, among his high-profile clients, even calling her his 'soul sister.'"
}
```

